constants.constant:
The "Create..." submenu of FileSystem dock's context menu, or the "New" section of the main context menu when empty space is clicked. [method _popup_menu] and option callback will be called with the path of the currently selected folder. When clicking the empty space, the list of paths for popup method will be empty.
[codeblock]
func _popup_menu(paths):
    if paths.is_empty():
        add_context_menu_item("New Image File...", create_image)
    else:
        add_context_menu_item("Image File...", create_image)
[/codeblock]

Context menu of Script editor's code editor. [method _popup_menu] will be called with the path to the [CodeEdit] node. You can fetch it using this code:
[codeblock]
func _popup_menu(paths):
	var code_edit = Engine.get_main_loop().root.get_node(paths[0])
[/codeblock]
The option callback will receive reference to that node. You can use [CodeEdit] methods to perform symbol lookups etc.

Context menu opened by an unmodified right-click in the 3D editor viewport. The clicked document is activated before the menu is built. [kbd]Ctrl + Right Mouse Button[/kbd] controls freelook, while [kbd]Alt + Right Mouse Button[/kbd] keeps the overlapping-node selection menu.
[method _popup_menu] receives paths to all editable [Node3D] nodes under the cursor. [method get_context] provides the click snapshot. A normal option callback receives the same [Dictionary].
The dictionary contains [code]viewport[/code], [code]viewport_index[/code], [code]camera[/code], [code]scene_root[/code], [code]document_path[/code], [code]document_history_id[/code], [code]nodes[/code], [code]selected_nodes[/code], [code]viewport_position[/code], [code]screen_position[/code], [code]ray_origin[/code], [code]ray_direction[/code], [code]placement_position[/code], [code]placement_source[/code], and [code]physics_hit[/code]. When [code]physics_hit[/code] is [code]true[/code], it also contains [code]hit_position[/code], [code]hit_normal[/code], [code]collider[/code], [code]collider_id[/code], [code]collider_rid[/code], [code]shape[/code], and [code]face_index[/code].
[code]placement_source[/code] is [code]&"physics"[/code], [code]&"ground_plane"[/code], or [code]&"view_plane"[/code].
[codeblock]
func _popup_menu(paths):
    var context := get_context()
    if context.scene_root:
        add_context_menu_item("Print Click Position", _print_click_position)

func _print_click_position(context):
    print(context.placement_position)
[/codeblock]
